# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Boi Bondhu — frontend configuration
#
# PROXY MODE (what is deployed): the browser calls /api/* on its own origin and
# next.config.ts forwards it to API_PROXY_TARGET. No CORS, no TLS on the backend,
# and the HTTPS Vercel page never talks to the plain-HTTP EC2 box directly.
#
#   local:  API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000      (default, can stay unset)
#   Vercel: API_PROXY_TARGET=http://13.48.12.56:8000    (set in the dashboard)
#
# API_PROXY_TARGET is read at build time, so changing it needs a redeploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DIRECT MODE (optional, only with an HTTPS API domain)
#
# If you later put Caddy + a domain in front of the backend (docker compose
# --profile tls), set this instead, in the Vercel dashboard:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.your-domain
#
# Leave it unset to keep proxy mode. It is inlined into the browser bundle at build
# time, so it also needs a redeploy. A localhost value is ignored on a deployed host.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
